      "repair_reason": "- [P1] Maintainer or contributor handling is needed because the branch should be re-scoped or closed; an automated repair would mostly revert the proposed behavior rather than finish a valid fix.; Needs attention: The diff changes exec approval parsing and has concrete security-boundary concerns around misclassifying wrapper operands as executables.; Review finding: [P1] Keep flock option separators before the lock... (sha=fe5e06d5556885a33e96dc3856179549bbb57e7d)",
      "review_summary": "The PR changes dispatch-wrapper parsing so `flock <lock> -- <command>` skips the separator and `script -- ...` treats the following tokens as command-only.\n\nPR surface: Source +5. Total +5 across 1 file.\n\nReproducibility: yes. for the PR defect: source inspection shows the new branches unwrap `flock <lock> -- ...` and command-only `script -- ...`. A live util-linux `flock` check rejects the after-lock separator, and BSD/macOS script docs keep the first positional token as the transcript file.",
